CSV pipeline + evidence-based filter

Two coupled changes. The scraper swap is a prerequisite for the filter's only validated exclusion, so do it first.

Part A: swap the DOM scrape for the CSV download

Repurpose, do not rebuild

data-windows/scripts/tv_export.py already does this and is hardened. It produced the 547-file corpus every number below is measured on. It carries fixes for traps that are not obvious:

"Go to" is the only chart control used. Range tabs let TradingView pick its own resolution and it silently switches to 1M, overriding interval=D. Zooming does the same.

One browser per ticker, torn down after each download. Reusing a chart and swapping the symbol keeps the previous view's loaded range, so a later symbol exports truncated history that still looks valid (AMZN came back 704 bars vs 2203 on a clean load).

Process-parallel, not threads - Playwright's sync API is bound to its creating thread.

storage_state auth, not a shared profile - a Chromium user-data dir is locked to one process.

Every file verified from the FILE (check(), line 104): ncols >= MIN_COLS, nrows >= MIN_ROWS, and median bar gap <= MAX_BAR_GAP_DAYS. The bar-spacing check exists because a coarser interval reaches FURTHER back, so it passes a naive depth check by looking better rather than worse. Failures go to _suspect/, never into the panel.

Resumability via done_tickers(), plus --workers / --limit / --tier / --tickers / --outdir.

What today's scraper does, and what changes

devin-s/src/data/tv_scraper.py does three things per ticker: a chart screenshot, a Data Window DOM scrape into <ticker>_datawindow.json, and a disabled zoom shot. The DOM scrape (line 325) depends on [data-test-id-value-title] selectors, a mouse-move to the bottom-right to snap the crosshair onto the latest bar, and an EXPECTED_MIN_FIELDS count.

Replace only the Data Window scrape. Keep the screenshot - the agent uses the chart image for pattern context.

What the CSV buys:

No DOM dependency. Selectors, crosshair positioning and field-count heuristics all disappear.

Exact numerics instead of parsed display strings.

History for free - this is the point. Trailing bars make ret_10d and realvol_10d computable, and those are the only features that separate on the screener population.

Format parity with the corpus, so the filter can be replayed against 1.9M historical bars for validation.

Adapter keeps everything downstream working

process_survivor.py consumes <ticker>_datawindow.json in two places - it passes the dict to triage_ticker (line 289) and also reads raw label strings directly for the LLM payload (lines 529-628). Do not break either.

Write csv_to_datawindow(csv_path) -> (snapshot: dict, history: DataFrame):

snapshot = the last row, keyed by the CSV header names, matching the shape parse_data_window already accepts. _FIELD_LABELS matching is substring/alnum-based, so header names like "RR To Target" resolve without change.

history = the trailing rows for the new exclusion.

Keep writing <ticker>_datawindow.json from snapshot so the LLM payload path is untouched.

Note the CSV column order is about to change if the plot-sort is done; everything reads by header name, so that is safe.

Design
flowchart TD
    CSV[TradingView CSV] --> ADP[csv_to_datawindow]
    ADP --> SNAP[snapshot = last row]
    ADP --> HIST[history = trailing bars]
    SNAP --> P[parse_data_window]
    HIST --> HF[realvol_10d, ret_10d]
    P --> V{core fields present?}
    V -->|no| BAD[CUT bad_data]
    V -->|yes| X{hard exclusions}
    HF --> X
    X -->|hit| CUTX[CUT + reason]
    X -->|clear| R{code 20 REVERSAL BUY?}
    R -->|yes| PASSR[PASS: HIGH if rev>=10 else MED]
    R -->|no| W[WATCH, ordered by tiebreak]
Hard CUT (each significantly negative in both eras, plus safety):
- Ext Pct vs MA200 >= 25
- price >= P_RICH and HV20 >= HV_HIGH
- realvol_10d >= 42.8 or ret_10d >= 12.9%
- action code in {17 PARABOLIC, 18 TOXIC}
- Stage == 0 (Hull MA not converged; ~25% of a listing's first 150 bars)
Soft demote to WATCH: codes 11/12/13/16/19, Ext Z >= 1.5, MTF 3/3.The single PASS lane: action == 20, conviction HIGH when rev_l >= 10, else MED.Everything else is WATCH, ordered by an explicitly unvalidated tiebreak_score(). Its docstring must say it is era-dependent and exists to make the DEEP_RESEARCH_CAP cut deterministic, not because it predicts.Do not gate PASS on codes 1/2 - not significant in either era, and adding it to a working screen collapsed +0.36 to +0.08.Sides: long-only for PASS (short codes 1/2 are structurally impossible - f_finalizeActionShort demotes every one to WATCH). Emit the short read as context and keep short_plan populated.API compatibility
Four callers: process_survivor.py (x2), deep_research.py, run_local_research.py, scripts/triage/retriage_datawindows.py. Keep exact signatures for triage_ticker, run_data_window_filter, parse_data_window, decode_action, action_is_actionable, rank_pass_tickers, deep_research_sort_key, normalize_number_str, _CORE_FIELDS, _BEAR_MASK_BITS, _REV_MASK_BITS, _WEAK_MASK_BITS.Verdict dict must keep every consumed key: triage, chosen_side, mode, reason, conviction, rr, ev_r, win_prob, in_zone, flags, regime, rev, recency, long_plan, short_plan, pursue, pursue_reason, news_negative, sentiment. Compute ev_r/win_prob locally from Dir Prob + RR To Target per bible section 8.4 rather than reading cut exports.Traps to encode

- RR To Target is the dominant side's ratio, not always the long.
- Long RR Valid reads 1 on 88.8% of bars that have no zone at all - never a standalone quality gate.
- Read exported Long In Zone; do not recompute zbot <= price <= ztop (the real test is ATR-tolerant on one side).
- The anchor name can be stale relative to a moved zone - never infer a price from it.
- full_v2 predates the $1 sentinel fix; exclude Long Entry == 0 bars when replaying.
Open risk
Every figure is measured on all bars or on the Long Ignition proxy, never on true screener output. The proxy is underpowered (21,600 bars, CI roughly +/-0.4), so the design is "unproven", not "disproven". The fix is the durable log in the final todo - after a few hundred alerts, re-run the whole analysis on the real population.
